   "Hyperbolic Structure Arising from a Knot Invariant",
   "Kazuhiro HIKAMI \u2020"
  ],
  "abstract": "We study the knot invariant based on the quantum dilogarithm function. This invariant can be regarded as a non-compact analogue of Kashaev\u2019s invariant, or the colored Jones invariant, and is de\ufb01ned by an integral form. The 3-dimensional picture of our invariant originates from the pentagon identity of the quantum dilogarithm function, and we show that the hyperbolicity consistency conditions in gluing polyhedra arise naturally in the classical limit as the saddle point equation of our invariant.",
